  "slug": "basal-ganglia-29a7",
  "summary": "Donor-scale single-nucleus atlases now pair cell abundance, expression, and genetic variation with ageing and Alzheimer's disease across brain regions.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is single-cell and single-nucleus profiling of basal ganglia and related brain regions, resolved at donor scale to separate cell-type abundance from expression variation. A striatal study of 3.9M nuclei from 178 donors quantifies abundance and expression variation with age and common eQTLs, with open data. A harmonized resource of cortical and hippocampal transcriptomes from wild-type and Alzheimer's disease model mice addresses reuse of public mouse snRNA-seq data by standardizing sample metadata. A prefrontal cortex multi-omic QTL atlas from 231 donors links brain disorder genetic risk to cell-type and developmental gene regulation. The HypoAD atlas pairs MRI from 458 people with 614,403 snRNA-seq nuclei to map hypothalamic volume and cell-type changes in ageing and Alzheimer's disease. The scCVD database integrates scRNA-seq and scATAC-seq across 701 cerebrovascular samples. New here is the pairing of donor-scale sampling with cell-type-resolved regulatory and imaging readouts, while tissue and disease focus varies across these studies.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
